# Quick Implementation Guide

## Step-by-Step: Securing Your Express App

### Step 1: Install Dependencies
```bash
npm install helmet express-rate-limit express-validator cors morgan dotenv
```

### Step 2: Create Environment File
Create `.env`:
```env
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000
ALLOWED_ORIGINS=http://localhost:3000
```

Add to `.gitignore`:
```
.env
node_modules/
```

### Step 3: Add Security Middleware (Top of app.js)
```javascript
require('dotenv').config();
const express = require('express');
const helmet = require('helmet');
const rateLimit = require('express-rate-limit');
const cors = require('cors');
const morgan = require('morgan');

const app = express();

// Security headers
app.use(helmet());

// CORS
app.use(cors({
  origin: process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS?.split(',') || ['http://localhost:3000']
}));

// Rate limiting
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 100
});
app.use(limiter);

// Body parsing with limits
app.use(express.json({ limit: '10kb' }));
app.use(express.urlencoded({ extended: true, limit: '10kb' }));

// Logging
app.use(morgan('combined'));
```

### Step 4: Add Input Validation
```javascript
const { body, query, param, validationResult } = require('express-validator');

// Validation error handler
const validate = (req, res, next) => {
  const errors = validationResult(req);
  if (!errors.isEmpty()) {
    return res.status(400).json({
      status: 'error',
      errors: errors.array()
    });
  }
  next();
};

// Example: Validate route
app.get('/users/:id', [
  param('id').isInt({ min: 1 }),
  validate
], (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    // Your code here
  } catch (error) {
    next(error);
  }
});
```

### Step 5: Add Error Handlers (Bottom of app.js)
```javascript
// 404 handler
app.use((req, res) => {
  res.status(404).json({
    status: 'error',
    message: 'Route not found'
  });
});

// Global error handler
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  console.error(err);
  res.status(err.statusCode || 500).json({
    status: 'error',
    message: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production' 
      ? 'An error occurred' 
      : err.message
  });
});
```

### Step 6: Graceful Shutdown
```javascript
const server = app.listen(process.env.PORT || 3000, () => {
  console.log(`Server running on port ${process.env.PORT || 3000}`);
});

process.on('SIGTERM', () => {
  server.close(() => {
    console.log('Server closed');
    process.exit(0);
  });
});
```

### Step 7: Test Your Security
```bash
# Run security audit
npm audit

# Test your endpoints
curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/health
curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/users
curl -X GET http://localhost:3000/users/abc  # Should return 400
```

## Common Validation Patterns

### Email Validation
```javascript
body('email')
  .trim()
  .isEmail().withMessage('Invalid email')
  .normalizeEmail()
```

### String Validation
```javascript
body('name')
  .trim()
  .notEmpty()
  .isLength({ min: 2, max: 50 })
  .matches(/^[a-zA-Z\s-']+$/)
  .escape()
```

### Integer Validation
```javascript
param('id')
  .isInt({ min: 1 })
  .toInt()
```

### Date Validation
```javascript
body('birthdate')
  .isISO8601()
  .toDate()
```

### Custom Validation
```javascript
body('username')
  .custom(async (value) => {
    const user = await User.findByUsername(value);
    if (user) {
      throw new Error('Username already exists');
    }
    return true;
  })
```

