curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/users \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"name":"<script>alert(\"XSS\")</script>","email":"test@test.com"}'
```

## Security Checklist

- [ ] All user inputs are validated and sanitized
- [ ] Rate limiting is configured
- [ ] Security headers are set (helmet)
- [ ] Errors don't leak sensitive information
- [ ] Authentication is implemented for protected routes
- [ ] HTTPS is enforced in production
- [ ] CORS is properly configured
- [ ] Secrets are stored in environment variables
- [ ] Database queries use parameterized statements
- [ ] Passwords are hashed with bcrypt
- [ ] Request logging is enabled
- [ ] Graceful shutdown is implemented
- [ ] Dependencies are regularly updated
- [ ] Security audits are performed (`npm audit`)

## OWASP Top 10 Coverage

1. ✅ **Injection** - Input validation and parameterized queries
2. ✅ **Broken Authentication** - JWT/session authentication recommended
3. ✅ **Sensitive Data Exposure** - Don't leak errors, use HTTPS
4. ✅ **XML External Entities (XXE)** - JSON only, validate content type
5. ✅ **Broken Access Control** - Authorization checks recommended
6. ✅ **Security Misconfiguration** - Helmet, secure defaults
7. ✅ **Cross-Site Scripting (XSS)** - Input sanitization with validator
8. ✅ **Insecure Deserialization** - JSON parsing with size limits
9. ✅ **Using Components with Known Vulnerabilities** - Regular npm audit
10. ✅ **Insufficient Logging & Monitoring** - Morgan request logging

## Resources

- [Express Security Best Practices](https://expressjs.com/en/advanced/best-practice-security.html)
- [OWASP Top 10](https://owasp.org/www-project-top-ten/)
- [Node.js Security Checklist](https://github.com/goldbergyoni/nodebestpractices#6-security-best-practices)
- [Helmet Documentation](https://helmetjs.github.io/)

