## 12. Brute Force Attack

### Attack Example
```bash
# Attacker tries many passwords
for pass in $(cat passwords.txt); do
  curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/login \
    -d "{\"username\":\"admin\",\"password\":\"$pass\"}"
done
```

### Protection in Improved Code
```javascript
// Rate limiting per IP
const limiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 100
});

// Additional: Account-specific rate limiting (recommended)
const loginLimiter = rateLimit({
  windowMs: 15 * 60 * 1000,
  max: 5, // Only 5 login attempts
  skipSuccessfulRequests: true,
  message: 'Too many login attempts, please try again later.'
});

app.post('/login', loginLimiter, (req, res) => {
  // Login logic...
});

// Additional: Account lockout after failed attempts
const MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS = 5;
const LOCK_TIME = 15 * 60 * 1000; // 15 minutes

// Track in database or Redis
if (user.failedLoginAttempts >= MAX_FAILED_ATTEMPTS) {
  if (Date.now() - user.lastFailedLogin < LOCK_TIME) {
    return res.status(429).json({
      error: 'Too Many Requests',
      message: 'Account temporarily locked due to too many failed attempts'
    });
  }
}
```

